     ],
     "excerpt": "A manufacturer must investigate and notify the regulator if a model's annual thermal-incident rate exceeds 10 per 100,000 installed units. A mandatory recall is triggered when a regulator, after reviewing the evidence, determines that the model presents an unreasonable safety risk; the incident-rate threshold alone prompts review and does not automatically trigger recall.",
     "comparison": "Permanent recall trigger of 10/100k is above the 8/100k maximum and recall is left to regulator discretion (weakened S5, benefiting Halcyon). Together with m6's weakened S2 it proposes a cross-section trade giving each company a section weakened below the acceptable range."
    }
